    <statement><p>(a) Set up a double integral for calculating
the flux of the vector field
<m>\vec{F}(\vec{r}) = \vec{r}</m>,
where <m>\vec{r} = \langle x,y,z \rangle</m>,
through the part of the upward oriented surface 
<m>z = 2(x^2+y^2)</m> that lies above the disk
<m>x^2 + y^2 \leq 25</m>.</p>
<p>Flux = <m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_{Disk}</m>
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>dx \, dy</m></p>
<p>(b) Evaluate the integral.</p>
<p>Flux = 
<m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_S \vec{F} \cdot d\vec{A}</m> =
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <hint/>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-2\pi }{2}\cdot 5^{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
